        "type": "label",
        "content": "CHATUCHAK WEEKEND MARKET"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "With more than 15,000 shops and 200,000 visitors every Saturday and Sunday, Bangkok’s Chatuchak"
      },
      {
        "type": "sentence",
        "content": "Weekend Market is a popular place with visitors to Thailand. You can find plants, flowers, music, jewelry,"
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "content": "clothes, food, and even animals!"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "The market is a great place to find bargains, and prices are generally low. Most people bargain, but some"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "don’t, so don’t worry if you don’t want to bargain. Just go with a friendly smile and have enough cash in your"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "pocket. There are ATMs for cash, but they are difficult to find, and many vendors don’t take credit cards."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "The market is huge, and many people walk in circles, even with a map. Don’t try to see it all in one day!"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "The market is open from 8:00 to 6:00 Saturday and Sunday. It’s good to get there early, before it gets too"
      },
      {
        "type": "sentence",
        "content": "busy. Wear light, comfortable clothing and bring a bottle of water. And for lunch, try some of Thailand’s"
      },
      {
        "type": "sentence",
        "content": "famous snacks, such as fried scorpions!"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "The market is very easy to get to. It’s only a five-minute walk from Mo Chit station on Bangkok's Skytrain."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Many people come by train but leave by taxi. It's easier to get your purchases back to your hotel that way!"
      },
